  "inference": "Because process_one_work clears PENDING before calling the work function, schedule_work may queue one follow-up execution while the current worker runs; additional notifications coalesce while that follow-up is pending. The GV100 teardown first blocks and removes a wait=true notifier whose callback is protected by the event-list read lock, then disables the buffer interrupt and flushes work before releasing the buffer. The shared NVKM allocator sizes the instance-memory ring from the hardware entry count and pins it through BAR2. The v7.0 interrupt path routes the MC fault bit to the GV100 handler under the core interrupt lock. The non-replayable register fault is decoded, sent synchronously to FIFO recovery, then acknowledged; replayable buffer events schedule work only when the matching buffer exists. FIFO recovery itself is an architecture callback.",
  "limitations": [
    "Upstream Linux source analysis only; Ubuntu module source-package equivalence is unknown.",
    "This does not validate GPU producer memory ordering, ring overflow behavior, or hardware interrupt delivery; no explicit DMA barrier is established by these source checks.",
    "The audited source explicitly acknowledges the non-replayable fault bit after synchronous FIFO dispatch; it does not establish how replayable buffer status is acknowledged by hardware or other code.",
    "This is Nouveau behavior, not NVIDIA Resource Manager implementation or ABI proof.",
    "No driver module was loaded and no GPU or CUDA execution was used."
  ],
